# Feedback-resume subscription seed (FT-032 / ADR-025).
#
# Seeded into the orchestration store by `dec init` alongside the
# verifier-dispatch subscription. Triggers a `resume_check` call for
# every paused `dec:DispatchGroup` whose `dec:blockedBy` references a
# `dec:Feedback` that has just reached a terminal lifecycle state
# (`addressed`, `rejected`, or `closed`).
#
# - oxi:selectQuery : every (group, feedback) pair where the group is
#                     parked in `paused-for-feedback` and the linked
#                     feedback's `dec:lifecycleState` is terminal. The
#                     handler dispatches `core::dispatch::resume_check`
#                     per row; resume_check itself is idempotent.
# - oxi:mode "sync" : the handler runs in-process — the resume call
#                     either advances the group back to `awaiting-action`
#                     (retry path) or to `feedback-rejected-action-blocked`
#                     (terminal failure mode).
# - oxi:handler     : opaque tag the harness binds to
#                     `core::subscriptions::feedback_resume::handle`.
#
# Idempotency: `resume_check` reads the group's current status and is a
# typed no-op when the group is not in `paused-for-feedback`, so repeated
# evaluations of this subscription cannot produce duplicate transitions.

@prefix oxi:  <https://decision-cli.dev/oxi-events/ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<https://decision-cli.dev/ns/subscription/feedback-resume>
    a oxi:Subscription ;
    rdfs:label "feedback resume check (terminal feedback unblocks paused dispatch)" ;
    oxi:selectQuery """PREFIX dec: <https://decision-cli.dev/ns#>
SELECT ?group ?feedback WHERE {
  ?group a dec:DispatchGroup ;
         dec:dispatchStatus \"paused-for-feedback\" ;
         dec:blockedBy ?feedback .
  ?feedback dec:lifecycleState ?state .
  FILTER(?state IN (\"addressed\", \"rejected\", \"closed\"))
}""" ;
    oxi:mode "sync" ;
    oxi:handler "feedback-resume" .
